{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/4941-played-mummy","id":4941,"title":"Played Mummy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T03:56:26-08:00","id":4941,"title":"Played Mummy?","content":"I was wondering if anyone here had actually played a Mummy game through, curious to see how it plays? I've got the book (from the Kickstarter), but my group is in the middle of an Exalted game at the moment, and doesn't seem to want to change anytime soon. Which is fine. Exalted is a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> I notice that, in contrast to other game lines, you start at 10 &quot;power stat&quot;, with the potential that implies, but the same attributes/skill distribution as in others. Does anyone find that to be a bump, that as your characters raise their Attributes or Skills, they get bumped down by their decreasing Sekhem? Or is it not really an issue?<br /> <br /> Any other good/bad points, or warnings/advice for running the first game in it, things you learned that you wish you'd known to begin with or would have made things smoother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T04:36:49-08:00","id":4954,"title":"","content":"When employing flashbacks, note what the characters' Sekhem and Memory scores are <i>in the flashback</i>, seperately. And keep the notes, in case you want to return to that time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T05:36:58-08:00","id":4984,"title":"","content":"Ive been running it since January. Ive ran the SAS in the core book twice, most recently at LA By Night. Being this is initally a game of very powerful beings some feedback I got was to have the powers pre-printed and handed out so players can know what their Arisen can do. Setting wise I would recommend having some active Arisen in the nome that can help in the social aspects of the game. Guildhalls will help alot in this as this is info that is not in the core book. <br /> <br /> Dave, that is good advise on flashbacks. I have not run one yet but I am planning on it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}